{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>But if the woman has not been defiled.</b> By this hiding — [she is cleared]." "<b>And she is clean.</b> From another place." "<b>And she shall be cleared.</b> From the bitter waters — and not only that, but <b>and she shall retain seed</b> — if she used to give birth in pain, from now she gives birth in ease; if she used to give birth to dark ones, from now she gives birth to fair ones."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:36.967323104Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}